[OC]|cffffffffThe Stockade|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, dungeon range 24-32 (Icy Veins, Method), mobs 23-29 in the DB, ~25-30 min (Method says 15-25 for a geared group). Bosses, all elite: Targorr the Dread 24, Dextren Ward 26, Kam Deepfury 27, Hamhock 28, Bazil Thredd 29, plus the rare Bruegal Ironknuckle 26. Bring the tank friend and a healer, you two are the damage. Everything is picked up outside and nothing hands in inside; the door is in the city, so a food or repair run mid-dungeon is a one-minute walk
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r the Forever DB gives the levels, drops, quests and item stats; the layout and boss tactics are from the Forever guides (Icy Veins, Method, Warcraft Tavern) and Classic-era knowledge, not verified on this server. Warcraft Tavern calls it unchanged from Classic except the loot
[OC]|cffffcc00Your quests:|r
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r The Stockade Riots (391) - the Head of Bazil Thredd - |cff66ff66normal|r, last boss of the right wing. Not shareable: everyone who wants it needs 389 done and 391 in the log
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Quell the Uprising (387) - 10 Defias Prisoners, 8 Convicts and 8 Insurgents (elite 23-26) - |cff66ff66normal|r on a full clear, they are most of the trash; the DB has no spawn counts, so if you are short at the end, clear what you skipped. Shareable
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r The Color of Blood (388) - 10 Red Wool Bandanas - |cff66ff66normal|r: eight types drop them (Prisoner, Captive, Inmate, Convict, Insurgent, Dextren Ward, Bazil Thredd, Bruegal) but the DB has no drop rate, so expect to finish around Dextren or Bazil and keep killing if not. Shareable
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r What Comes Around... (386) - the Head of Targorr - |cff66ff66normal|r, first boss. Hands in to Guard Berton in Lakeshire (chapter 16)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Crime and Punishment (377) - the Hand of Dextren Ward - |cff66ff66normal|r, end of the left wing. Hands in to Councilman Millstipe in Darkshire (chapter 17)
[OC]|cffffcc00Not now:|r The Fury Runs Deep (378, Kam Deepfury's head, 2,750 XP) needs The Dark Iron War at Dun Modr first (chapter 19) and the head is a quest drop, so Kam gives you nothing for it today. Come back for him only if you want a second run

|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Gather at the door beside Warden Thelwater and enter The Stockade [G52.4,70.0 Stormwind City]
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00In a group:|r pet on passive, Growl OFF, send it at the tank's target only. Freezing Trap is your crowd control: the guides want the side Defias controlled before each boss pull
[OC]|cffffcc00The cell block|r  -  T-shaped: the hallway straight ahead is Targorr's (he stands in one of several cells off it), the left wing ends at Dextren Ward with the rare Bruegal on the way, the right wing holds Kam, then Hamhock, then Bazil Thredd. The wings go in either order; this route is Targorr, left, right, so Bazil is last and the walk out is one corridor
[OC]|cffffcc00The trash|r  -  every pack is elite Defias, 23-26. Captives cast Infected Wound (more physical damage taken) and Inmates cast Rend, which hits harder on a wounded target: kill Captives and Inmates first. Convicts Backhand (a stun), Insurgents shout (Demoralizing Shout cuts your attack power). Pull small and keep the rooms apart: Targorr's adds can be pulled from the neighbouring cells in the first hallway
[OC]|cffffcc00Targorr the Dread|r (24 elite orc, first boss, in one of several cells with 1-3 Defias): he dual-wields, Thrash gives him extra swings and he enrages at low health (guides say 20-30%). Tank and spank: adds first, tank builds threat, healer on the tank
Kill [TAR1696 Targorr the Dread] and loot the Head of Targorr [QC386]
[OC]|cffffcc00Bruegal Ironknuckle|r (26 rare, left wing, not always there): no abilities of note, the adds round him are the danger. Tank and spank
[OC]|cffffcc00Dextren Ward|r (26 elite, end of the left wing): Intimidating Shout is an area fear. Clear every cell near his room first and pull him where a fear cannot carry you into another room; |cff66ff66shaman: drop Tremor Totem before the pull|r, it breaks the fear (Method)
Kill [TAR1663 Dextren Ward] and loot the Hand of Dextren Ward [QC377]
[OC]|cffffcc00Kam Deepfury|r (27 elite Dark Iron dwarf, a cell in the right wing): Shield Slam stuns his target for 2 seconds and hits hard, and Improved Blocking raises his block for 6 seconds. The healer watches the tank through each stun, DPS wait a few seconds for threat. Adds first
[OC]|cffffcc00Hamhock|r (28 elite ogre mage, at the end of the wing with 2 Defias): Chain Lightning is interruptible and he Bloodlusts himself and his adds (+30% speed, purgeable). Kill the two Defias, then interrupt him and purge the Bloodlust (shaman: Earth Shock and Purge), and stay spread so the chain jumps less
[OC]|cffffcc00Bazil Thredd|r (29 elite, last boss of the right wing and the end of this route): dual-wields and hits hard; Smoke Bomb stuns everyone near him for 4 seconds, so ranged players keep their distance and the healer tops the tank off first. Sources disagree on adds, so clear the room before you start
Kill [TAR1716 Bazil Thredd] and loot the Head of Bazil Thredd [QC391]
Check the tallies: kill whatever Defias you still need before you leave [QC387] [QC388]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot calls (rolls):|r |cff66ff66Graverobber's Shovel|r (Dextren: 2H mace 23.0 dps +12 AP +10 Sta, req 23, unique) - ROLL, the Reef Axe / Twilight Maul tier; |cff66ff66Kam's Walking Stick|r (staff 17.7 dps +10 Agi +3 Int +32 spell damage) beats the Spider Leg staff but trails the 22-23 dps 2H axes and maces. |cff66ff66Defender's Leather Helm|r (+12 Str +13 Sta, req 25; Dextren, Kam or Bazil) is still your helm call, skip it if you took one in Blackfathom. |cff66ff66Defias Jailbreakers|r (Bazil: gloves +6 Agi +7 Sta, req 26) unless your gloves carry 6+ Agility; |cff66ff66Blackrock Harness|r (Targorr: chest +14 AP +8 Sta +4 Defense, req 21) if your chest is weaker; |cff66ff66Executioner Mantle|r (Targorr: shoulders +10 AP +9 Spi) if your shoulders have no AP; Demolition Girdle (Kam: +8 Str +9 spell damage) only over a weak belt, Moss Cinch is the same tier; Combat Cloak (Bazil, BoE +6 Sta +2 Spi, req 27) for a bare cloak slot. Pass: Boneslicer (a polearm), the Concealed Hand Crossbow, Hamhock's Cleaver, Ogre Grips (mail), Repurposed Rack (a shield), Dark Horde Band, Prison Shank, Iron Knuckles and the caster pieces
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Loot calls (rolls):|r |cff66ff66Concealed Hand Crossbow|r (Bazil: 15.3 dps +12 ranged AP, req 26) beats the Naga Heartpiercer and the Fallenroot Longbow if you shoot crossbows (the skill is a weapon trainer's). |cff66ff66Brawler's Leather Helm|r (+10 Agi +13 Sta, req 25; Dextren, Kam, Hamhock or Bazil) is still your helm call. |cff66ff66Defias Jailbreakers|r (Bazil: gloves +6 Agi +7 Sta, req 26) unless your gloves carry 6+ Agility. If you trained Staves (Woo Ping): |cff66ff66Kam's Walking Stick|r (+10 Agi +3 Int) is your best Agility stick. Combat Cloak (Bazil, BoE +6 Sta +2 Spi, req 27) for a bare cloak slot. Pass: Boneslicer (no stats), the Shovel (hunters cannot use maces), Hamhock's Cleaver, Ogre Grips (mail), Repurposed Rack, the Attack Power chest and shoulders, Prison Shank and Iron Knuckles
[OC]|cffffcc00Trash loot (both):|r |cff66ff66Defias Renegade Ring|r (+4 Agi +6 Sta, req 21, unique) drops from the five Defias types: take it for an empty or weak ring slot, the Ring of Precision from Blackfathom is the same tier. Superior Boots (Targorr, Kam, Bruegal) are leather boots with a random enchantment: read the suffix before you roll

